  subject to public ridicule.

* Signing up to play on a public server is not a
  relinquishment of personal privacy.

* I don't approve of snooping, and my already
  rampant paranoia makes me get twitchy when I feel
  like people are watching over my shoulder, whether
  in real time or otherwise.

* Signing up to a public server isn't an instance
  of volunteering to be an instructor or to create
  instructional materials. The implied agenda for
  signing on to play NetHack on a public server ends
  at "play the game NetHack".

Many more could be written, those should suffice.

